# Flash Sale Purchase Feature

## Problem Statement

We need to add a purchase feature to the Flash Sale module.

## Business Rules

* A user can purchase only one unit during a flash sale period.
* A user can only make one purchase per flash sale.
* If the number of reserved or sold units reaches the available stock, further purchase requests must be rejected.
* Purchase processing must be handled asynchronously using BullMQ.
* The implementation must prevent overselling caused by concurrent requests.

---

# Implementation Plan

## 1. Database Changes

### Create Purchase Entity

Create a new entity named `Purchase` in:

```text
/src/entities/purchase.entity.ts
```

Table name:

```text
purchases
```

### Properties

| Property     | Type   | Nullable | Notes                             |
| ------------ | ------ | -------- | --------------------------------- |
| id           | UUID   | No       | Primary key                       |
| status       | enum   | Yes      | `processing`, `done`, `failed`    |
| message      | string | Yes      | Error message if processing fails |
| purchaseCode | string | Yes      | Generated purchase identifier     |
| createdAt    | Date   | No       | TypeORM CreateDateColumn          |
| updatedAt    | Date   | No       | TypeORM UpdateDateColumn          |

### Relationships

A purchase belongs to exactly one user and one flash sale.

#### Purchase → FlashSaleEntity

```typescript
@ManyToOne(() => FlashSaleEntity)
flashSale: FlashSaleEntity;
```

#### Purchase → UserEntity

```typescript
@ManyToOne(() => UserEntity)
user: UserEntity;
```

