# Expected Purchase Flow

```text
User calls POST /flash-sale/purchase
            │
            ▼
Start Database Transaction
            │
            ▼
Load Flash Sale
            │
            ▼
Load User
            │
            ▼
Count Purchase Records
(status = processing OR done)
            │
            ▼
Validate Stock
            │
            ▼
Validate Duplicate Purchase
            │
            ▼
Generate Purchase Code
            │
            ▼
Create Purchase (processing)
            │
            ▼
Persist Purchase
            │
            ▼
Commit Transaction
            │
            ▼
Publish BullMQ Job
            │
            ▼
Return Purchase Response
            │
            ▼
BullMQ Consumer
            │
            ▼
Send Email
            │
            ▼
Update Purchase Status
        done / failed
```

# Acceptance Criteria

## Success Case

* User can purchase a flash sale item.
* Purchase record is created with status `processing`.
* Purchase creation is performed inside a database transaction.
* Transaction commits successfully before BullMQ job publication.
* BullMQ job is published successfully.
* Email is sent successfully.
* Purchase status becomes `done`.

## Duplicate Purchase

* User attempts to purchase the same flash sale more than once.
* API returns HTTP `409 Conflict`.
* No additional Purchase record is created.

## Sold Out

* Number of Purchase records with status `processing` or `done` reaches available stock.
* API returns HTTP `409 Conflict`.
* No additional Purchase record is created.

## Concurrency

* Concurrent purchase requests cannot oversell inventory.
* Total Purchase records in status `processing` or `done` never exceed available stock.

## Processing Failure

* Email sending or purchase processing fails.
* Purchase status becomes `failed`.
* Error message is stored in the `message` field.

## Queue Consistency

* Every BullMQ job references a Purchase record that already exists in the database.
* No BullMQ job is published before the corresponding database transaction is committed.
